**IMPORTANT**: Generate ONLY the RunList React component. This is a presentation component for displaying build runs.

# GOAL
Create a React component that displays a list of Convex build runs with status badges and details.

# CONTEXT
This component receives run data from Convex and displays it in a clean, readable format with color-coded status badges.

# STACK
- React
- TypeScript
- Inline styles (no CSS imports)

# ARTIFACTS
- `components/RunList.tsx`: Build run list component (implementation only, no tests)

# FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
- Accept runs prop of type Run[]
- Display each run as a card with:
  - Spec name as heading
  - Color-coded status badge with emoji
  - Summary text in gray box
  - Duration and cost on right side
  - Start/end timestamps at bottom
  - Attempt count if > 1
- Use status colors:
  - planning: blue (#3b82f6, bg #eff6ff, emoji 📋)
  - building: orange (#f59e0b, bg #fffbeb, emoji 🔨)
  - testing: purple (#8b5cf6, bg #f5f3ff, emoji 🧪)
  - done: green (#10b981, bg #ecfdf5, emoji ✅)
  - error: red (#ef4444, bg #fef2f2, emoji ❌)

# INTERFACE
```typescript
import { Id } from '../convex/_generated/dataModel';

interface Run {
  _id: Id<'runs'>;
  specName: string;
  startedAt: number;
  endedAt?: number;
  status: 'planning' | 'building' | 'testing' | 'done' | 'error';
  summary: string;
  totalCost?: number;
  attempts?: number;
}

interface RunListProps {
  runs: Run[];
}

export default function RunList({ runs }: RunListProps) {
  // Implementation
}
```

# HELPER FUNCTIONS
Include these utility functions:
- formatDate(timestamp: number): string - converts to locale string
- formatDuration(startedAt: number, endedAt?: number): string - shows duration or "Running..."
- formatCost(cost?: number): string - shows "$X.XXXX" or "Free"

# VERIFICATION
✅ Accepts runs array prop
✅ Displays all run details
✅ Color-codes status badges correctly
✅ Shows duration, cost, attempts
✅ Formats timestamps properly
✅ Clean responsive layout
